  "discussion": "A short period north northwest swell will gradually lower today. Meanwhile, an overlapping, moderate, mid- to long period northwest swell will continue to build and bring surf to near advisory levels along north and west facing shores Tuesday into Wednesday. A small north northeast swell should arrive during the second half of the week. Overlapping south-southwest swells will keep surf along south-facing shores slightly above average through Tuesday. A slightly larger south swell may bring an additional bump to the surf Thursday and Friday. Surf along most east-facing shores will be small through early this week, but areas exposed to wrapping northerly swells will experience periods of moderate surf today. East-facing shores should also see a bump in surf if the north-northeast swell materializes during the latter half of this week.",
